findings.comment:
750.800b - The following food contact surfaces were soiled:
A) fry baskets and tongs (grease/food debris) - left from previous operating day in main kitchen;
B) can opener blade (general buildup);
C) coffee maker spout above grounds basket (buildup);  and
D) small ice machine (mold) - juncture where baffle and ceiling meet.

Clean and sanitize food contact surfaces between uses/as needed to prevent cross contamination and eliminate buildup of debris. In-use equipment (i.e. knives, cutting boards, can opener, etc.) must go through ware washing process up to every 4hrs after continuous use.

750.800e - The following non-food contact surfaces were soiled:
A) (R) counter under pizza ovens (food debris);
B) counter under coffee maker (food/dust/debris);
C) under popcorn machine (food debris);
D) drain line to soda gun (pink mold);
E) drain for ice machine condensate line (mold);
F) table holding flat grill in side kitchen (dust/debris);
G) grease shoot of flat grill (grease buildup);
H) bottom inside stand alone oven (carbon/buildup);
I) drip trays beneath char-grill and stove-top burners (food splash/carbon);
J) under microwave in side kitchen (dust/food debris);
K) shelving in side kitchen (splash/dust);  
L) ledge beneath condenser in prep cooler (debris/puddling condensation);  and
M) plastic dividers on shelves in alcohol walkin (mold).

Clean non-food contact surfaces daily/as needed to eliminate buildup of debris.

findings.citation_text:
750.1220 -  Floors were soiled in the following  areas:
A) corner by 3 part sink at banquet room bar (old mouse droppings/debris);
B) side kitchen - along walls under equipment (food/debris);
C) under ice machine (debris);  and
D) alcohol walkin (around kegs - spilled/hardened liquid/broken glass).

Clean the floors as needed to eliminate buildup of debris.
